  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "4441e859-7c94-40f8-bd4f-eb75f808b8d7",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        560,
        96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Track mandatory paid leave with Gemini, Gmail and Google Sheets\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs monthly to check whether employees are on track to take their mandatory paid leave. It reads employee and leave-record data from Google Sheets, calculates each employee’s leave deadline and shortfall, filters those at risk, and uses Gemini to draft a personalized notification. It then emails the employee, sends HR a Slack summary, and logs the notification back to Google Sheets.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the schedule trigger to run on the desired monthly cadence, such as the first day of each month.\n- Set the leave-rule values in the configuration node, including spreadsheetId, grantMethod, fixedGrantMonthDay, and requiredDays.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and ensure the employee list, leave records, and notification log sheets have the expected columns.\n- Connect Google Gemini credentials for the LLM chain, Gmail credentials for employee emails, and Slack credentials plus target channel for HR summaries.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the leave calculation code, risk filter criteria, Gemini prompt, email wording, Slack destination, or sheet column mappings to match company policy and local leave requirements."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d1aac9fc-9536-4193-8048-86a80e90d7c9",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1136,
        208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Schedule leave rules\n\nStarts the workflow on a monthly schedule and defines the core leave policy settings used by the rest of the process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9255b54e-a0be-4d63-ad45-2f26b0721762",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1584,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 528,
        "height": 528,
        "content": "## Load and combine records\n\nThe employee list and the leave records are merged on employee ID.\nKeep Everything is used on purpose, so people who have taken no\nleave at all are not dropped — they are the ones most at risk."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "75559486-f8df-44aa-8b6c-fa4269d48a7b",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1136,
        544
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 432,
        "height": 432,
        "content": "## Calculate leave risk\n\nLeave is granted six months after the hire date, then annually, so\nevery employee has a different deadline. Set grantMethod to\nfixed_date if your company grants leave to everyone on the same day.\nOnly employees granted ten days or more are covered by the rule."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a39adc21-86db-4dce-98e2-292ecc3e862e",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1648,
        640
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 352,
        "height": 464,
        "content": "## Draft employee message\n\nThe prompt is written in English so it is easy to review and edit,\nwhile the messages themselves are generated in Japanese for the\nstaff who receive them."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
